Greg's STANDING authorization for forced cleanup removal on Windows B (2026-11-22 ~22:25Z, relayed verbatim by Engram::Asistant, TermAl mailbox 588693a8 #2565): „tak, koniecznie!” ("yes, absolutely!"), answering Fable2's question #2564. That question asked whether the Codex runner on Windows B may remove the residue of the launcher's private test userprofile with `Remove-Item -LiteralPath <path> -Recurse -Force`. This satisfies AGENTS.md "Cleanup deletions" ("Forced removal requires Greg's recorded authorization for that exact case") for that case, and ONLY within the four limits of #2564:
(1) literal in-repository paths under .tmp/j/ or the short temp dirs .tmp/i* on Windows B;
(2) only AFTER the non-forced form (Remove-Item -LiteralPath -Recurse -Confirm:$false without -Force) has failed;
(3) only after the same guards: the run is terminal with its outcome recovered, retention has ended, no link escapes the path, and nothing live uses it;
(4) a record of each removal (paths, time, free space) on the disk-sweep item w-b92d241c0154.
It grants nothing else: no other host, no other path, no ACL or attribute changes outside that removal, and no forced git worktree remove.
